---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 How Spark Handles Partitions vs. Cores
Partitions: Spark splits your dataset into logical chunks. Each partition becomes a task.

Cores: Each core can run one task at a time.

 What Happens
If partitions < cores → not all cores are used, some sit idle.

If partitions = cores → perfect utilization, all cores busy.

If partitions > cores → Spark queues tasks. Each core runs one task, then picks up the next until all are finished.
